    },
    {
      "id": "WOuZqD5fbDGjncFkldR1G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -714.4325170551476,
      "y": 264.0472931079824,
      "width": 997.8988037109375,
      "height": 324,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1254898661,
      "version": 730,
      "versionNonce": 1530239915,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788464014564,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ACC Enrollment Flow\n1. Choose \"Seller Central\"\n2. Enter Seller Central merchant token\n3. We verify the token matches an Amazon Ads Profile attached to the organization\n4. Wayward displays a managed Amazon email address\n5. User invites that email as a Seller Central user\n6. User pastes the Amazon invitation link into Wayward\n7. Wayward accepts the invitation\n8. User grants that email \"View\" permission for Creator Connections\n9. User clicks the permission-check button in Wayward\n10. Wayward enters the correct Seller Central account, opens Creator Connections, and discovers ACC entityId\n11. Connection becomes ACTIVE",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ACC Enrollment Flow\n1. Choose \"Seller Central\"\n2. Enter Seller Central merchant token\n3. We verify the token matches an Amazon Ads Profile attached to the organization\n4. Wayward displays a managed Amazon email address\n5. User invites that email as a Seller Central user\n6. User pastes the Amazon invitation link into Wayward\n7. Wayward accepts the invitation\n8. User grants that email \"View\" permission for Creator Connections\n9. User clicks the permission-check button in Wayward\n10. Wayward enters the correct Seller Central account, opens Creator Connections, and discovers ACC entityId\n11. Connection becomes ACTIVE",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "1mSaOxeq8kdkvBZfp48lR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -689.0800526202089,
      "y": 671.0950336941419,
      "width": 722.3590698242188,
      "height": 270,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 990254987,
      "version": 412,
      "versionNonce": 900526667,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788464143015,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Summary - user provides 3 values\n1. Merchant token: tells Wayward which Seller Central seller is being connected\n2. Invitation link: gives Wayward Amazon user access to that seller\n3. Creator Connections permission: allows user to view ACC data\n\n\nWayward automatically discovers\n1. Matching Amazon Ads profile(s)\n2. ACC entityId\n3. Creator Connections campaigns and reporting data",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Summary - user provides 3 values\n1. Merchant token: tells Wayward which Seller Central seller is being connected\n2. Invitation link: gives Wayward Amazon user access to that seller\n3. Creator Connections permission: allows user to view ACC data\n\n\nWayward automatically discovers\n1. Matching Amazon Ads profile(s)\n2. ACC entityId\n3. Creator Connections campaigns and reporting data",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "Hk7qX2YHOzVVxBa0kSdp8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -645.0122647561635,
      "y": 1054.6912814135028,
      "width": 573.019287109375,
      "height": 297,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 11763211,
      "version": 22,
      "versionNonce": 514552421,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788464158364,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "  For BACTRACK, it fails at step 3–4:\n\n  User enters BACTRACK merchant token\n          ↓\n  Wayward confirms BACTRACK owns matching Ads profiles\n          ↓\n  Wayward tries to create the setup record\n          ↓\n  An older hidden connection already owns that merchant token\n          ↓\n  “Seller Central account is already connected”",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "  For BACTRACK, it fails at step 3–4:\n\n  User enters BACTRACK merchant token\n          ↓\n  Wayward confirms BACTRACK owns matching Ads profiles\n          ↓\n  Wayward tries to create the setup record\n          ↓\n  An older hidden connection already owns that merchant token\n          ↓\n  “Seller Central account is already connected”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "jEoi2lWFS3REhIVaZHWa9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -600.1252728208996,
      "y": -749.4113561934914,
      "width": 836.458984375,
      "height": 864,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1341916677,
      "version": 245,
      "versionNonce": 280975691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788537978856,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Normal Seller Central setup, step by step\n\nThe customer opens Creator Connections setup from one of their Wayward brand accounts.\n\nThe route resolves that account to its owning Wayward organization; the resulting\nconnection belongs to the organization, not just the one UI account.\n\nThe customer copies the merchant token from Seller Central and enters it in Wayward.\nWayward checks its imported Amazon Ads profiles. At least one seller_account under\nthat same Wayward organization must have that exact merchant identity. This prevents a\ncustomer from claiming an unrelated seller merely by knowing its token.\n  - Connect would verify that any profile had the seller merchant across ALL orgs. I\n\nWayward creates a creator_connection in PENDING_INVITE and assigns the least-loaded\nactive Wayward-managed Amazon login. A global unique index permits only one connection\nfor the merchant identity, because two would fetch and attribute the same economics\ntwice.\n\nThe UI tells the customer which Wayward Amazon email to invite. The customer creates a\nuser invitation in Seller Central and pastes the invitation link into Wayward.\n\nA workflow signs in as the assigned managed login and accepts the invitation. The row\nadvances to AWAITING_PERMISSION.\n\nThe customer grants that invited user View access to Creator Connections in Amazon.\nA second check enters the seller-scoped Amazon context, proves access, discovers the ACC\nentity, and advances the row to ACTIVE.\n\nScheduled fetching uses the ACC entity and managed login. Raw campaign changes are\nstamped with creator_connection_id; reporting joins that id back to the connection's\ncurrent organization.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Normal Seller Central setup, step by step\n\nThe customer opens Creator Connections setup from one of their Wayward brand accounts.\n\nThe route resolves that account to its owning Wayward organization; the resulting\nconnection belongs to the organization, not just the one UI account.\n\nThe customer copies the merchant token from Seller Central and enters it in Wayward.\nWayward checks its imported Amazon Ads profiles. At least one seller_account under\nthat same Wayward organization must have that exact merchant identity. This prevents a\ncustomer from claiming an unrelated seller merely by knowing its token.\n  - Connect would verify that any profile had the seller merchant across ALL orgs. I\n\nWayward creates a creator_connection in PENDING_INVITE and assigns the least-loaded\nactive Wayward-managed Amazon login. A global unique index permits only one connection\nfor the merchant identity, because two would fetch and attribute the same economics\ntwice.\n\nThe UI tells the customer which Wayward Amazon email to invite. The customer creates a\nuser invitation in Seller Central and pastes the invitation link into Wayward.\n\nA workflow signs in as the assigned managed login and accepts the invitation. The row\nadvances to AWAITING_PERMISSION.\n\nThe customer grants that invited user View access to Creator Connections in Amazon.\nA second check enters the seller-scoped Amazon context, proves access, discovers the ACC\nentity, and advances the row to ACTIVE.\n\nScheduled fetching uses the ACC entity and managed login. Raw campaign changes are\nstamped with creator_connection_id; reporting joins that id back to the connection's\ncurrent organization.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "8ZubOwa21BfdKSTbTmzjQ",
